Subject: [PATCH] Lichii #1028: async read-back (the reading thread waits for its own buffer downloads), early downloads of read-back pages, and a narrower wait for DMA snapshot misses (EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK, EDEN_UP_L1028_EARLY, EDEN_UP_L1028_DMA_WAIT, EDEN_UP_L1028_VERIFY, EDEN_UP_L1028_DMA_WAIT_VERIFY, EDEN_UP_L1028_STATS; all off by default)

Port of zortos293/Lichii #1028 (egla91/async-readback-nx2, merged into nx2 as 0b83798bf6 on 9 Nov;
"video_core: async read-back: the reading thread waits for its downloads (port of #805's
read-back)"). Commits by jpkto and zortos293 (Zortos); capy-ai co-authored most of them, claude
co-authored df7e7da097, d020b62d91 and 027514b2c3. Measured upstream (5900X + RTX 3080, EGLA-91
round 4, no profiler, fresh launch per run): Ocarina of Time at Kokiri 28.2 -> 32.9 fps (+17%,
p90 38.0 -> 32.8 ms), Donkey Kong Bananza unchanged; with the GPU profile (round 2) the back
thread's fence waits went 117 -> 0 ms/s in Ocarina; the narrower macro DMA wait alone did not
shorten Ocarina's front wait there (235 -> 250 ms/s).
To be numbered 0482 (after 0481 lichii-949-drain-free-acquire; T84 = 0001..0481).

