Batch 1: c, v, r, d, c. Stop there if v logs a "Lichii #1028 verify:" or "Lichii #1028 DMA wait
check:" line, its 10 s line shows "differ" or "GPU-modified bytes no download brought" above 0 or
"DMA wait ... verify differences" above 0, any run hangs ("GPU split wait on the back thread",
"Waited ... s for the GPU thread to submit tick") or crashes. Batch 2: c, u, r, d, c. Batch 3: c, u,
u, then d or r (whichever is still open), c. A p arm (EDEN_NX2_PREFLUSH=0 alone) only if u is
clearly off c: it tells EARLY's share from preflush's.
Proof the switch acted: r/u: the 10 s line says "async on", synced reads 0, async reads ~ c's synced
reads (2.6-3.6/s), "fell back" 0; u: "early on", early downloads > 0, "only waited for a download
on its way" > 0; d/u: "dma wait on", the narrower-wait count > 0 and SPLIT_WAITS shows the "dma
snapshot writes" site. Calls: d wins only if it beats its same-batch controls in two batches with
back idle down; retire d if the narrower waits are under ~25% of the misses (the rest drain
anyway). r is the cost check (expected = c): if r runs > 0.3 fps under c in two batches, read u
against r, not c.
Readouts: walk fps mean and 1% low, flashes/min, pond load OK; "Lichii #1028 read-back per
second": c: synced reads/s and ms, GPU thread in their flushes, host GPU waits under the buffer
