Review (9 Nov, adversarial pass; original kept as lichii-1028.diff.pre-review). Fixed: (a) the
landing check after every collected guest write (a seq_cst fence each, upstream's choice) now runs
only when Collect stored new bits; a run of writes into one 64-byte block fences once (deviation
above; unset unchanged). (b) WaitForHostRead read the split front's own Active flag from guest
threads; it asks BackRunning now (EARLY only reaches it). Header: risks 8 and 9, the expectations
(ASYNC_READBACK's cost, DMA_WAIT tempered by t74-d and upstream), PREFLUSH=0's history, the batch
plan (at most 5 a batch, v as the gate), the stacking. Checked, no change needed: unset = T84 (every
new path behind a static false test, an empty container or g_read_downloads 0; the seven
ClearDownload -> ClearReplacedDownload sites run the old body when no read download exists); lock
order (the query cache takes the buffer lock, never the reverse; GatherAndApply holds its mutex
only around the gather, whose callback takes no cache lock; a guest thread in Await holds no lock a
landing needs); landings serialise under the buffer lock (the fence pops hold it); no thread waits
on the host GPU for an unsubmitted tick except a reader (EARLY), which asks the back; the DMA wait's
positions and pages are the notes' (device addresses, write position after the entry), its
QueryDma calls are no-ops at SyncMode 0, which it requires; every gpu_modified_ranges add marks the
Nx2 table (MayHoldGpuWrites). Re-run: lichii-1028_review_checks.sh + lichii-1028_review_inject.py
(VM scratch /tmp/l1028-rev-9q4k, log lichii-1028.review-checks.log).

